    "updated_at": "2026-11-12T11:11:51Z",
    "body": "Refreshed with the refreshed #1141 (34bb4413), #1136 (18dcf446, which already carries #1131 50e395e8) and upstream/main (6a10c5ad). All three merged cleanly. Head 26b3d962.\n\nWhat changed:\n- The Machine window's EDM section now follows #560's condition rules. `problems()` judges each condition with the loader's own `condition_refusal` (now public in `post::machine`, next to `condition_id_key`), so the page names the rule Apply would hit, in the loader's words: the id is a word with no surrounding spaces, gap > 0, and undersize is in (0, 1] mm. Ids are compared the way the loader compares them, ignoring case and leading zeros (\"S1\"/\"s1\" and \"01\"/\"1\" are one selector). A wire-only `wire_diameter` on a sinker condition is also named.\n- Ticking a condition's gap or undersize now seeds 0.01 mm or 0.1 mm, values the loader accepts. It used to seed 0, which the new law refuses.\n- \"Add condition\" skips ids that collide under the loader's key.\n- Pin: `sinker_machine_tests::problems_name_each_law_the_loader_keeps` was extended. For every new rule (gap 0, undersize 0 and 1.5, case and leading-zero id collisions, a spaced id, an empty id) it asserts that the page names the problem and that `Edm::is_sane` refuses it. For the wire field it asserts that `Machine::edm_sane` refuses it. It also checks that the seeds pass both.\n- PROCESS_VERSION 31, carried from #1141.\n\nTests: ui `sinker_setup` 1/1, ui lib `sinker_machine` 6/6 (`sinker` filter 9/9), app `solid_law_goldens` 5, `sinker_burn` 10, `edm_conditions` 1, `edm_machine` 5, post lib 38, all green. `clippy -D warnings` is clean on post, app and ui (all targets). Still a draft.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
